BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Qi-Gong with Cody
DTSTART;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260704T080000
DTEND;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260704T090000
UID:9c779c0b09140c3606eeaed9a218bec5@wellnesscollectivemoab.com
DESCRIPTION:Zhineng Qigong is a powerful mind-body practice rooted in anci
 ent Chinese healing traditions and adapted for modern times. This gentle y
 et profound system blends slow movement\, sound\, visualization\, and medi
 tation to help individuals cultivate inner peace\, restore balance\, and e
 nhance vitality. By consciously connecting with the energy of life—what 
 some may call qi or universal life force—participants are invited into a
  process of holistic healing: physically\, emotionally\, and spiritually. 
 One of the most accessible forms of Qigong\, Zhineng emphasizes connection
  over complexity. Its principles can be embraced by people of all ages\, b
 ackgrounds\, and physical abilities. Cody teaches from a place of lived ex
 perience\, having found this practice deeply healing and transformative in
  his own journey. His classes focus on cultivating shared energy through g
 roup practice\, empowering individuals to tap into their innate wisdom and
  live with greater purpose and presence.
LOCATION:Wellness Collective\, 76 S 100 W\, Moab\, UT 84532
X-SOURCE:Wellness Collective Moab
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chair Yoga with Breann
DTSTART;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260706T090000
DTEND;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260706T100000
UID:c92a22c8c38089e678c6cd8b681f4641@wellnesscollectivemoab.com
DESCRIPTION:Chair Yoga – Mondays at 9 AM Join us every Monday morning at
  9:00 AM for a gentle and accessible Chair Yoga class\, led by Breann\, a 
 certified trauma-sensitive yoga teacher and experienced massage therapist.
  Breann brings over 20 years of experience in guiding others toward greate
 r body awareness\, healing\, and relaxation. This class is designed for ev
 eryone – whether you are new to yoga\, have limited mobility\, or are lo
 oking for a mindful and soothing way to start your week. Chair Yoga allows
  you to experience the benefits of yoga without needing to get down on a m
 at. What to Expect: • Seated and standing postures using the chair for s
 upport • Gentle stretches to enhance flexibility • Breathing exercises
  to calm the mind and body • Movements to promote better circulation and
  balance ✨ No experience necessary – come as you are! Where: Wellness 
 Collective When: Every Monday at 9:00 AM Cost: By donation Let this practi
 ce be a moment of self-care and grounding in your week.
LOCATION:Wellness Collective\, 76 S 100 W\, Moab\, UT 84532
X-SOURCE:Wellness Collective Moab
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tai Chi with Drew
DTSTART;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260706T171500
DTEND;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260706T181500
UID:79c893a4c76492c07a30246bd86e0447@wellnesscollectivemoab.com
DESCRIPTION:Among all forms of physical activity\, Tai Chi Ch’uan is per
 haps the most accessible\, convenient\, and economical way to improve both
  physical health and mental well-being. As Yang Style Tai Chi master Cheng
  Man-Ching once said\, ‘Those who understand the importance of exercise 
 for health will find Tai Chi Ch’uan indispensable.’ While Tai Chi may 
 not be easy to master\, consistent practice will yield results. In this cl
 ass\, we will focus on cultivating chi\, building endurance and strength\,
  and developing core alignment\, all while learning to release tension. Ta
 i Chi training offers many levels of progression. In Yang Style\, when pra
 cticed correctly\, it becomes an aerobic workout\, despite minimal movemen
 t. Additionally\, it serves as a form of meditation. Please wear comfortab
 le clothing. Flat shoes\, socks\, or bare feet are ideal. Students are enc
 ouraged to train at their own pace\, and progression will vary from person
  to person.
LOCATION:Wellness Collective\, 76 S 100 W\, Moab\, UT 84532
X-SOURCE:Wellness Collective Moab
END:VEVENT
